    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0744" n="732" xml:id="pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Lieutenant General Alvan C. Gillem, Jr., to Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-05">April 5, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You asked that I inform you when Communist members of Field Teams had gone into
                    Manchuria. I am now informed by Mr. Robertson that 40 Communist Team members
                    proceeded to Mukden on 2 April 1946.</p>
                <closer><signed>A. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gillem, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
